 "title": "GIS | Lancaster County, NE",
 "text": "GIS | Lancaster County, NE\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\n-->\nDepartments\nBusiness\nTourism\nCounty Services\nHow Do I...\nSearch\nHome\nDepartments\nA through C\nAssessor/Register of Deeds\nGIS\nGIS\nOverview\nGIS Viewer/Property Search\nResources\nOverview\nGIS, or Geographic Information System, is a technology that enables the collection, analysis, and visualization of geographic data. GIS systems help manage spatial information, aiding in decision-making, land use planning, environmental management, and property assessment. By integrating data from various sources, GIS provides powerful insights into geographic patterns and trends.\nWe have implemented an advanced Geographic Information System (GIS) to enhance our property mapping and data management. Our system includes improved cadastral mapping capabilities, which play a crucial role in accurately determining equalized market values for properties. The GIS system is a valuable tool for both public access and internal analysis, helping ensure transparency and consistency in property assessments.\nGIS Viewer/Property Search\nProperty Information Map (GIS Viewer)\nOur GIS Viewer provides an interactive map that allows you to access detailed property information, view cadastral data, and explore geographic features. The map helps users visualize property boundaries, assess value changes, and make informed decisions based on up-to-date information.\nGIS Viewer Help\nNeed help navigating the new GIS Viewer? Click on the Help tab in the left panel of the application for how-to's and information.\nResources\nDownload GIS Data\nWe provide access to GIS data that includes important geographic and property information. You can download the most recent GIS datasets for personal use, analysis, and planning.\nPID Scheme\nThe Property Identification (PID) Scheme (PDF) is a structured system for assigning unique property identifiers that help streamline property management and data tracking. The PID scheme ensures that each property is accurately represented in the GIS system, which facilitates property assessments, data retrieval, and land management.\nContact Us\nDouglas Guess\nGeospatial Administrator\nEmail\nChad Kendall\nGeospatial Developer\nEmail\nKimberly Haman\nGeospatial Technician II\nEmail\nMikal Stewart\nGeospatial Analyst\nEmail\nMike Jones\nGeospatial Technician II\nEmail\nJobs\nOnline\nPayments\nAssessor\nBudget\nCorrections\nAgendas &\nMinutes\nMarriage Licenses\nTreasurer\nCourts\nReport Road\nIssues\n-->\nLANCASTER COUNTY WEATHER\nContact Us\n555 S 10th Street\nLincoln, NE 68508\nStaff Directory\nHELPFUL LINKS\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nSite Map\nWork for Lancaster County\nNewsroom\nHome\nLancaster County Bid & Business Opportunities\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\n[]\nPageAssist\nDiscover your personalization options\nClose ×",
